/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1389 */
/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1218 — hero stack-front gradient (higher-specificity override)
   Ship #1215 pinned `body .csfloat-home-hero-feature-stub.stack-front`
   to a blue gradient, but a LATER rule in the same stylesheet
   carries the canonical magenta gradient at the more-specific
   selector
       .csfloat-home-hero-stack .csfloat-home-hero-feature-stub.stack-front
   so #1215's `body .stub.stack-front` (specificity 0,2,1) loses
   to that selector (0,3,0) — even with !important the cascade
   tiebreaker is selector-strength, and an earlier !important
   rule loses to a later !important rule of equal-or-higher
   specificity. The pink stripe in the centre of the hero card
   is the result. Match the higher-specificity selector exactly
   and append it AFTER the offender so this rule wins on the
   later-declared tiebreak. Keep the same csfloat-blue palette
   from #1215; #1216 already covers the surrounding radial wash. */
body .csfloat-home-hero-stack .csfloat-home-hero-feature-stub.stack-front {
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    rgb(28, 32, 48) 0%,
    rgb(30, 36, 58) 45%,
    rgb(32, 56, 100) 56%,
    rgba(35, 123, 255, 0.55) 60%,
    rgba(35, 123, 255, 0.55) 62%,
    rgb(28, 70, 140) 78%,
    rgb(20, 36, 80) 100%
  ) !important;
  background-color: rgb(28, 32, 48) !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1218 */
/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1219 — hero stack-back/stack-mid gradient (defensive)
   The stack-front sits on top of two stack-back / stack-mid
   layers in the .csfloat-home-hero-stack. If those backing
   cards inherit the same magenta-stop gradient as the original
   stack-front (likely — they were authored as a set), they'd
   bleed pink edges around the front card even after #1218
   muted the main face. Pin .stack-back and .stack-mid to the
   same csfloat-blue gradient family with slightly deeper
   tones so the back layers read as supporting depth shadows
   rather than competing colour. Defensive — even if the back
   layers were already neutral, this keeps them locked to the
   blue palette through any future style drift. */
body .csfloat-home-hero-stack .csfloat-home-hero-feature-stub.stack-back,
body .csfloat-home-hero-stack .csfloat-home-hero-feature-stub.stack-mid,
body .csfloat-home-hero-stack .csfloat-home-hero-feature-stub.stack-rear {
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    rgb(20, 24, 38) 0%,
    rgb(22, 28, 48) 50%,
    rgb(20, 36, 80) 100%
  ) !important;
  background-color: rgb(20, 24, 38) !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1219 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1390 — rarity GRADIENT OVERLAY on grid-thumb (csfloat parity)
   csfloat .container measured: linear-gradient(rgba(27,29,36,0) 20%, rarity-color@32%-alpha 100%)
   Image area 246x195, gradient fades transparent top → rarity color at bottom.
   sboxmarket has LEFT-edge 3px stripe (.grid-card::after) — wrong direction.
   Add a rarity-tinted vertical gradient OVERLAY to .grid-thumb that matches csfloat exactly.
   Standard=#3b82f6 blue, Off-Market=#e8b960 gold, Limited=#eb4b4b red. */
.grid-card .grid-thumb {
  position: relative !important;
}
.grid-card .grid-thumb::before {
  content: "" !important;
  position: absolute !important;
  inset: 0 !important;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg,
    rgba(27, 29, 36, 0) 20%,
    rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.32) 100%) !important;
  pointer-events: none !important;
  z-index: 0 !important;
  border-radius: inherit !important;
}
.grid-card:has(.rarity-Off-Market) .grid-thumb::before,
.grid-card:has(.grid-rarity.offmarket) .grid-thumb::before {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg,
    rgba(27, 29, 36, 0) 20%,
    rgba(232, 185, 96, 0.32) 100%) !important;
}
.grid-card:has(.rarity-Limited) .grid-thumb::before,
.grid-card:has(.grid-rarity.limited) .grid-thumb::before {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg,
    rgba(27, 29, 36, 0) 20%,
    rgba(235, 75, 75, 0.32) 100%) !important;
}
/* Suppress old left-edge 3px bar — csfloat doesn't have one. */
.grid-card::after {
  display: none !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1390 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #1391 — magnifier zoom button bottom-right of every thumb
   csfloat: 38x30 action buttons w/ bg rgba(30,32,38,0.55), 20x20 icons. sboxmarket
   has .grid-zoom — restyle to match csfloat chrome exactly. Bottom-right corner. */
.grid-card .grid-zoom {
